{"lines": ["Start with the reason these sounds exist at all. Deep in the ocean there is a layer of water where sound travels slower than anywhere above or below it. Sound bends toward that slow layer and gets trapped inside it. It is called the SOFAR channel, a deep sound channel, and low notes inside it can travel thousands of miles.", "Two teams found it independently in the nineteen-forties. Maurice Ewing and Lamar Worzel, in America. Leonid Brekhovskikh, in the Soviet Union.", "In 1944 they tested it. A microphone hung from a sailing ship called the Saluda. A second ship set off explosive charges up to nine hundred nautical miles away. About seventeen hundred kilometres. And the microphone heard them.", "Later, signals sent from a ship off Heard Island were picked up in parts of all five ocean basins. At Ascension Island, nine thousand two hundred kilometres away, they arrived about an hour and forty-four minutes later.", "Rule one. In the ocean, a sound can come from much farther away than you think."], "words": [["Start", 0.0, 0.22], ["with", 0.22, 0.4], ["the", 0.4, 0.5], ["reason", 0.5, 0.78], ["these", 0.78, 1.06], ["sounds", 1.06, 1.34], ["exist", 1.34, 1.72], ["at", 1.72, 1.98], ["all.", 1.98, 2.16], ["Deep", 2.82, 2.87], ["in", 2.87, 2.98], ["the", 2.98, 3.08], ["ocean", 3.08, 3.34], ["there", 3.34, 3.62], ["is", 3.62, 3.74], ["a", 3.74, 3.84], ["layer", 3.84, 4.06], ["of", 4.06, 4.22], ["water", 4.22, 4.5], ["where", 4.5, 4.76], ["sound", 4.76, 5.04], ["travels", 5.04, 5.48], ["slower", 5.48, 5.8], ["than", 5.8, 6.1], ["anywhere", 6.1, 6.42], ["above", 6.42, 6.84], ["or", 6.84, 7.1], ["below", 7.1, 7.34], ["it.", 7.34, 7.62], ["Sound", 7.98, 8.24], ["bends", 8.24, 8.5], ["toward", 8.5, 8.88], ["that", 8.88, 9.16], ["slow", 9.16, 9.4], ["layer", 9.4, 9.78], ["and", 9.78, 9.96], ["gets", 9.96, 10.12], ["trapped", 10.12, 10.4], ["inside", 10.4, 10.78], ["it.", 10.78, 11.16], ["It", 11.56, 11.7], ["is", 11.7, 11.78], ["called", 11.78, 12.04], ["the", 12.04,